# kk-daily-publish3-overseas — overseas window behind the podcast RSS gate (tasks 0323 R5,
# 0334 R1-R2; kk news verbs since 0369).
#
# 07:00 America/Los_Angeles, which needs no DST adjustment: the entry is defined in the zone the
# machine already runs in. The gated date is the PREVIOUS day, because the observed episodes land
# 13:43–15:22 PDT (after this tick) — `kk news publish` derives yesterday's LA date for
# `run_date` for this window.
#
# The gate decides whether anything publishes: a miss cancels the overseas targets and runs
# `diagnose` + the tier-0-only repair. This line carries no live consent; the overseas rows in the
# shipped preset are `draft`/`off`, so a live overseas post stays an operator launch.
#
# `kk news publish` owns the date math because a crontab command ends at the first UNESCAPED
# percent sign — an inline `date -v-1d +%Y%m%d` would truncate silently. The verb resolves the
# generation bundle from the effective works root and refuses a missing or mismatched bundle
# before it touches a channel.
#
# Rendered by `kk schedule render kk-daily-publish3-overseas --platform cron --repo <checkout>`;
# kk never edits the operator's crontab. MERGE, never replace:
#
#     crontab -l > /tmp/kk-overseas.cron 2>/dev/null || :
#     kk schedule render kk-daily-publish3-overseas --platform cron --repo "$PWD" >> /tmp/kk-overseas.cron
#     crontab /tmp/kk-overseas.cron
0 7 * * * cd {{repo}} && mkdir -p .works/kk-news-publish && PATH="{{home}}/.bun/bin:/opt/homebrew/bin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin:/usr/sbin:/sbin" TZ=America/Los_Angeles kk news publish --window overseas-rss --unattended >> {{repo}}/.works/kk-news-publish/overseas.log 2>&1
